IMPORT prelude

-- Parking Places Act 1974 (Singapore) -- heavy vehicles and the licence to park them (ss 2, 5), road parking places (s 4(2)),
-- private parking layouts and the deficiency charge (ss 6A, 6B), when a parking charge takes effect (s 9(5)), composition (s 12),
-- naming the driver (s 13), the owner's liability for parking offences (s 14), removal, clamping, release and sale of vehicles
-- (s 15), entry into private parking places (s 15B), penalties (ss 5A, 6A, 13, 15C, 16, 19) and personal immunity (s 20).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PPA1974.txt. The deposit
-- says it "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"; the latest amendment annotated is Act 12 of 2021
-- (s 13(3)).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 6 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules a driver, vehicle owner,
-- car-park operator or developer meets. Not encoded: administration and appointments (s 3), the Authority's powers to provide and
-- adapt parking places (ss 4(1), 6), the matters the Authority weighs on approvals and waivers (ss 6A(3), 6B(2)), how charges are
-- fixed and published (s 9(1)-(4)), collection (s 9A), traffic signs (s 11), shared-mobility removal and forfeiture (s 15(2), (8)-
-- (13)), information powers (s 15A), service (s 18), corporate and partnership liability (ss 17, 17A), exemptions beyond their
-- effect (s 21) and the rules (s 22). The deficiency charge amount, which offences are compoundable, and the parking offences
-- themselves are all left to rules, which were not retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Parking Places Act 1974 -- parking`

§§ `2 and 5 -- heavy vehicles and the licence`

-- s 2: "heavy vehicle" means (a) any heavy goods vehicle or concrete mixer, the maximum laden weight of which "exceeds 5,000
-- kilograms"; (b) any bus with a seating capacity of "more than 15 persons, not inclusive of the driver"; (c) any trailer, container
-- trailer, low loader or flat-bed trailer, maximum laden weight exceeding 5,000 kilograms; (d) any mobile crane or recovery vehicle,
-- the UNLADEN weight of which "exceeds 2,500 kilograms".
DECLARE VehicleKind IS ONE OF
    `a goods vehicle or concrete mixer`
    `a bus`
    `a trailer`
    `a mobile crane or recovery vehicle`
    `a car`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A VehicleKind, `maximum laden weight in kg` IS A NUMBER, `unladen weight in kg` IS A NUMBER, `seats excluding the driver` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the vehicle is a heavy vehicle` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a goods vehicle or concrete mixer` THEN `maximum laden weight in kg` GREATER THAN 5000
    WHEN `a bus` THEN `seats excluding the driver` GREATER THAN 15
    WHEN `a trailer` THEN `maximum laden weight in kg` GREATER THAN 5000
    WHEN `a mobile crane or recovery vehicle` THEN `unladen weight in kg` GREATER THAN 2500
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 5(1): "A person must not maintain or operate any private parking place for the parking or housing of one or more heavy
-- vehicles unless the person is a holder of a valid licence." A "private parking place" is land "owned or occupied by any person
-- other than the Government" (s 2). No special penalty: s 16 applies. s 21: the Minister may exempt any private parking place or
-- person "from the provisions of this Act".
GIVEN `operates a private parking place` IS A BOOLEAN, `it houses a heavy vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a valid licence` IS A BOOLEAN, `exempted by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `operating without a licence is an offence` IF
    `operates a private parking place` AND `it houses a heavy vehicle` AND (NOT `holds a valid licence`) AND (NOT `exempted by the Minister`)

§§ `4(2) -- parking places on a road`

-- s 4(2): the Authority "must not permit any part of a road to be used as a parking place" if (a) "the parking place is for the
-- parking of personal mobility devices"; or (b) it "will unreasonably prevent access to any premises adjoining the road" or to the
-- use of the road by anyone entitled to use it, "or will cause a nuisance to any person".
GIVEN `for personal mobility devices` IS A BOOLEAN, `unreasonably prevents access` IS A BOOLEAN, `causes a nuisance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority may permit road parking` IF
    (NOT `for personal mobility devices`) AND (NOT `unreasonably prevents access`) AND (NOT `causes a nuisance`)

§§ `6A and 6B -- private parking layouts and the deficiency charge`

-- s 6A(1): the owner or occupier must provide and maintain the private parking place "only in accordance with the applicable
-- requirements" if (a) the parking place is provided "on or after 8 May 2018"; or (b) development where (i) written permission is
-- granted on or after 8 May 2018 or (ii) an application for approval of a parking-lot plan "is pending on that date".
-- (5): contravening an infringement notice under (4): fine not exceeding $30,000 and, for a continuing offence, "a further fine
-- of $500" a day.
-- Dates are written as numbers YYYYMMDD (an encoding device, as in the stamp-duties row). 0 means "no such date".
GIVEN `parking place provided on` IS A NUMBER, `written permission granted on` IS A NUMBER, `application pending on 8 May 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 6A binds the owner or occupier` IF
        `parking place provided on` AT LEAST 20180508
    OR  `written permission granted on` AT LEAST 20180508
    OR  `application pending on 8 May 2018`

-- s 6B(1): the owner or occupier may provide lots "otherwise than in accordance with the requirements in rules" if (a) the
-- Authority waives the requirement because compliance would be "unduly onerous or unreasonable"; and (b) "where the waiver affects
-- the applicable number of parking lots, the owner or occupier pays to the Authority a deficiency charge".
-- (3): the amount is "calculated in the manner prescribed". (4): "no deficiency charge is payable" by a place or person exempt from
-- s 6A under s 21.
GIVEN `the waiver affects the number of lots` IS A BOOLEAN, `exempt from section 6A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a deficiency charge is payable` IF
    `the waiver affects the number of lots` AND (NOT `exempt from section 6A`)

GIVEN `the Authority waived the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN, `the waiver affects the number of lots` IS A BOOLEAN, `exempt from section 6A` IS A BOOLEAN, `paid the deficiency charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner may depart from the parking rules` IF
    `exempt from section 6A`
    OR (`the Authority waived the requirement` AND ((NOT `a deficiency charge is payable` `the waiver affects the number of lots` `exempt from section 6A`) OR `paid the deficiency charge`))

§§ `9(5) -- when a parking charge takes effect`

-- s 9(5): "No parking charge and no change to any parking charge has any effect until the notice relating to it is published in
-- accordance with subsection (4)" -- in the daily newspapers in all official languages, on the website, or otherwise as the
-- Superintendent considers adequate. (6): the instrument "does not have legislative effect".
GIVEN `notice published under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the parking charge has effect` IF `notice published under subsection (4)`

§§ `5A, 6A, 13, 15C, 16, 19 -- penalties`

-- s 16: contravening the Act or rules, "where no special penalty is provided": fine not exceeding $2,000 or imprisonment not
-- exceeding 3 months or both, and for a continuing offence a further fine not exceeding $500 a day. Sections 5(1), 10, 13(2), 15(6)
-- and 15(7) create offences without a penalty of their own, so s 16 applies to them.
-- s 5A(4): the same $2,000 / 3 months / $500 a day. s 6A(5): $30,000, no imprisonment, $500 a day. s 13(3) and s 15C(2): $10,000
-- or 12 months or both. s 19 (obstruction): $2,000 or 3 months or both, with no continuing fine.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `operating an unlicensed heavy-vehicle parking place`
    `ignoring a maintenance notice`
    `ignoring a layout infringement notice`
    `plying for hire in a parking place`
    `failing to name the driver`
    `giving false information about the driver`
    `giving false information in an application`
    `removing a clamped vehicle`
    `obstructing an officer`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `ignoring a layout infringement notice` THEN 30000
    WHEN `giving false information about the driver` THEN 10000
    WHEN `giving false information in an application` THEN 10000
    OTHERWISE 2000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `ignoring a layout infringement notice` THEN 0
    WHEN `giving false information about the driver` THEN 12
    WHEN `giving false information in an application` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 3

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the daily fine for a continuing offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `giving false information about the driver` THEN 0
    WHEN `giving false information in an application` THEN 0
    WHEN `obstructing an officer` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE 500

§§ `12 -- composition`

-- s 12(1)(a): the relevant officer may compound a PRESCRIBED compoundable offence by collecting "a sum not exceeding the lower of"
-- (i) "one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence"; (ii) "$5,000". (2): on payment "no further
-- proceedings are to be taken". Which offences are compoundable is prescribed elsewhere; this computes only the cap.
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that may be collected to compound` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`the maximum fine` `the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000

§§ `13 -- naming the driver`

-- s 13(1): where the driver is alleged to have committed an offence, "the owner of the vehicle must furnish any information
-- required ... as to the identity and address of the person who was the driver". (2): failing to furnish it "within 14 days after
-- the date on which the information was required" is an offence "unless he or she proves, to the satisfaction of the court, that he
-- or she did not know and could not with reasonable diligence have ascertained the information required".
-- `day furnished` counts days from the requirement; 0 means not furnished.
GIVEN `days since the requirement` IS A NUMBER, `day furnished` IS A NUMBER, `proved could not have ascertained it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to name the driver is an offence` IF
        `days since the requirement` GREATER THAN 14
    AND (`day furnished` EQUALS 0 OR `day furnished` GREATER THAN 14)
    AND (NOT `proved could not have ascertained it`)

§§ `14 -- the owner's liability for parking offences`

-- s 14(3)(a), (5): a declaration counts if made within 14 days after service (0 means none made) and about one offence only.
GIVEN `days` IS A NUMBER, `covers many` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the declaration counts` IF
    `days` GREATER THAN 0 AND `days` AT MOST 14 AND (NOT `covers many`)

-- s 14(1): when a parking offence is committed, the owner at the time "shall be guilty of an offence ... as if the person were the
-- actual offender" unless the Superintendent or the court is satisfied the vehicle was "a stolen vehicle or a vehicle illegally
-- taken or used". (3): nor if the owner (a) "within 14 days after service" of the notice "furnishes by statutory declaration" the
-- name and address of the person in charge; or (b), (c) satisfies the Superintendent or court that the owner "did not know and could
-- not with reasonable diligence have ascertained such name and address". (5): a declaration "which relates to more than one
-- parking offence" does not count.
GIVEN `the vehicle was stolen or illegally taken` IS A BOOLEAN, `days to make the declaration` IS A NUMBER, `the declaration covers more than one offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `owner could not have ascertained the driver` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner is liable for the parking offence` IF
        (NOT `the vehicle was stolen or illegally taken`)
    AND (NOT `the declaration counts` `days to make the declaration` `the declaration covers more than one offence`)
    AND (NOT `owner could not have ascertained the driver`)

-- s 14(2): "where a penalty has been imposed on or recovered from a person in relation to any parking offence, no further penalty
-- shall be imposed on or recovered from any other person in relation to that offence".
GIVEN `a penalty already imposed on someone for this offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a further penalty may be imposed` IF NOT `a penalty already imposed on someone for this offence`

-- s 14(6), "owner" of a registered motor vehicle: (a)(i) each registered owner unless the person "has sold or ceased to have
-- possession" and complied with the disposal rules; (ii) a sole or joint owner who is not registered; (iii) if the registered owner
-- has sold or ceased to have possession, anyone entitled to immediate possession; (d) for a vehicle under "a hiring agreement or
-- hire-purchase agreement, the person in possession or entitled to possession of the vehicle under that agreement".
-- (7): a person "is taken not to have ceased to have possession" where possession changes by (a) "any hiring (not being a hiring
-- under a hire-purchase agreement) or lending"; or (b) passing it to a bailee for sale, repair, storage and the like.
-- INFERENCE: read together, a car-rental hirer is an owner under (d) while the registered owner stays an owner under (a)(i) and
-- (7)(a); a borrower and a workshop are not owners.
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `the registered owner who kept the car`
    `the registered owner who lent the car`
    `a friend who borrowed the car`
    `the registered owner who hired the car out`
    `a rental hirer`
    `a hire-purchase hirer`
    `a workshop repairing the car`
    `the registered owner who sold the car and complied with the rules`
    `the buyer of the car`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is an owner` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `a friend who borrowed the car` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a workshop repairing the car` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the registered owner who sold the car and complied with the rules` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `15 -- removal, clamping, release and sale`

-- s 15(1): where a vehicle (a) appears "to have been abandoned without lawful authority" in a parking place; (b) "is parked in a
-- parking place in contravention of any provision of this Act or any rules"; or (c) "being owned by a person against whom a warrant
-- of arrest is in force, is parked in a parking place", the Superintendent or authorised officer may (d) remove and detain it or (e)
-- fix "an immobilisation device".
GIVEN `in a parking place` IS A BOOLEAN, `appears abandoned` IS A BOOLEAN, `parked in contravention` IS A BOOLEAN, `owner has a warrant of arrest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the vehicle may be removed or clamped` IF
    `in a parking place` AND (`appears abandoned` OR `parked in contravention` OR `owner has a warrant of arrest`)

-- s 15(4): it "must not be released to the owner ... except" (a) by or under the direction of the Superintendent or an officer;
-- and (b) "upon the owner of the vehicle having paid all expenses ... and any other charges"; (16): the Superintendent may waive
-- them. (5): where removed under (1)(c), release may be refused unless the owner "has been arrested or has surrendered" or the
-- warrant "has been cancelled by a court".
GIVEN `release directed by an officer` IS A BOOLEAN, `expenses paid or waived` IS A BOOLEAN, `removed for a warrant` IS A BOOLEAN, `owner arrested, surrendered or warrant cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the vehicle may be released` IF
        `release directed by an officer`
    AND `expenses paid or waived`
    AND ((NOT `removed for a warrant`) OR `owner arrested, surrendered or warrant cancelled`)

-- s 15(14): a vehicle not earlier forfeited and "not claimed by its owner within one month of the date of its detention or
-- immobilisation" may, "after giving one month's notice in the Gazette", be sold by public auction or otherwise disposed of.
-- (15): the surplus goes to the owner, or if unclaimed "within 12 months" is forfeited to the Authority.
GIVEN `months since detention` IS A NUMBER, `claimed by the owner` IS A BOOLEAN, `months since the Gazette notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the vehicle may be sold` IF
    `months since detention` GREATER THAN 1 AND (NOT `claimed by the owner`) AND `months since the Gazette notice` AT LEAST 1

§§ `15B -- entry into a private parking place`

-- s 15B(1): the Superintendent or an authorised person may "enter any private parking place between the hours of 8 a.m. and
-- 6 p.m." to survey or inspect. (2): not, "except with the consent of the owner or occupier", "without at least 6 hours' previous
-- notice". (3): where necessary or expedient to enter outside those hours, entry "by giving at least 6 hours' previous notice".
-- Hours are on a 24-hour clock.
GIVEN `hour of entry` IS A NUMBER, `hours of notice given` IS A NUMBER, `owner consents` IS A BOOLEAN, `necessary outside the hours` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may enter` IF
        (`hour of entry` AT LEAST 8 AND `hour of entry` AT MOST 18 AND (`owner consents` OR `hours of notice given` AT LEAST 6))
    OR  (`necessary outside the hours` AND `hours of notice given` AT LEAST 6)

§§ `20 -- protection from personal liability`

-- s 20: "No liability shall lie personally against" the Superintendent, deputies, enforcement officers and others "for anything
-- which is done or purported to be done, or omitted to be done, in good faith and with reasonable care".
GIVEN `acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `acted with reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is protected from personal liability` IF `acted in good faith` AND `acted with reasonable care`
